    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n72284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>accustomed to a fixed dwelling,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ζῴων τὰ μὲν οἰ. τὰ δὲ ἄοικα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					488a21
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>used as</i> or <i>suitable for a residence,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἰκία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PLond.</u>
					3.983.2
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iv A. D.)</span>, etc.</div>
